    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Everything passes. The full suite (one test class, `AcceptanceTest`) is green with `BUILD SUCCESS`, and the test itself round-trips `householdId` through create \u2192 GET, so the whole flow (OpenAPI generation \u2192 DTO \u2192 MapStruct \u2192 entity \u2192 DB) is verified end to end.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature on `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string to the `Owner` response schema (the write-only `sharesHousehold` flag on `OwnerFields` already existed). This generates `getHouseholdId`/`setHouseholdId` on the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java` model** \u2014 Added a `householdId` field mapped to a new `household_id` column, with getter/setter (mirroring `customerCode`). MapStruct auto-maps it to `OwnerDto`.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on `hsqldb`. Seed inserts use explicit column lists, so they're unaffected.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 When `sharesHousehold` is true and an existing owner already shares the household (same last name + address, case-insensitive with collapsed whitespace):\n   - the creation is allowed (existing conflict behavior preserved when the flag is false);\n   - a **stable shared** `householdId` is assigned \u2014 reusing any household member's existing id, otherwise deterministically derived as a 12-byte (24-hex) SHA-256 prefix of the normalized `lastName|address`;\n   - existing household members lacking an id are backfilled with the same value, so \"both\" owners share it.\n\nBecause the id is derived deterministically from last name + address, all owners in the same household resolve to the identical `householdId`, which is what the acceptance test asserts.",
